# 1. Project Overview

## 1.1 Project Summary

CLOAKID is a secure data-sharing platform designed to allow users to share sensitive information such as Personally Identifiable Information (PII) and Sensitive Personally Identifiable Information (SPII) in a controlled manner.

The system allows users to share data with verified individuals while applying redaction, access controls, expiry times, view limits, watermarking, activity monitoring, and the ability to revoke or modify access after sharing.

The sender retains control over shared data even after it has been shared.

## 1.2 Purpose, Scope and Objectives

### Purpose
The purpose of CLOAKID is to provide a secure and controlled method for sharing sensitive information between verified users.

### Scope
CLOAKID covers:
- Secure sharing of PII and SPII.
- Sharing between verified users.
- Redaction of sensitive portions of data.
- Encryption and secure transmission.
- Time-based and view-based access controls.
- Watermarking.
- Activity logging and monitoring.
- Access modification and revocation.
- Temporary storage followed by automatic deletion.

### Objectives
The system aims to:
- Prevent unauthorized access to sensitive information.
- Give the sender control over shared data.
- Restrict access according to time and number of views.
- Allow sensitive areas to be hidden or redacted.
- Track access and sharing activity.
- Delete shared data after the defined deletion period.

## 1.3 Assumptions and Constraints

### Assumptions
- Users have valid email accounts.
- The email address belongs to the user creating the account.
- Users have access to the internet and modern web browsers.
- The email notification system is functional.
- Users complete verification before using the system.

### Constraints
- Internet connectivity is required.
- Only verified users can send or receive data.
- Data is stored temporarily and deleted after the deletion time.
- Access is limited by time and number of views.
- Receivers cannot download or permanently store shared data.
- Resharing is disabled by default.
- Watermarking is required.
- User activities are logged.

